539b-aadc-437975100b51" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396647 1074 "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\nWe start by finding the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x\\pi }{2})=1$ for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x\\pi }{2} & =2m\\pi  \\\\ x & =4m,\\,m\\in Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the elements of $B$ for different values of $m,$ we have\n\n$$\nA={…,-4,0,4,8,…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. Since $A$ is infinite, and $A⊆B,$ it follows that $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊆C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\"" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396649 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396650 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396651 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396652 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396653 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396653 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396648 1080 #uuid "cc69c548-b178-59cf-a7e3-c85b144b3d40" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396649 1081 "$A$ and $C$ only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396649 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396649 1084 #uuid "08b646ac-4e89-5442-9a96-fda0b2f79464" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396650 1081 "$B$ and $C$ only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396650 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 1