. \n\nIf $f(x)=3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ then $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,3x=O(3x)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2x})=1$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(5x)$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line {{field-4}}  and \n{{field-5}}." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396723 1072 #uuid "e15b51c9-b3ac-5fdf-bdd1-db7479e393a2" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396723 1074 "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\n3x=O({{3x}_{⏟}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\n3x=O(3x),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line  $\\text{L4}$   we have\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=5,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396725 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396726 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396727 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396728 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396729 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1077 "field-3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396727 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396724 1080 #uuid "76168965-fb6c-530a-8fbd-b5a10cd9db80" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396725 1081 "the absorption property" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396725 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396725 1084 #uuid "e527463f-8290-5ced-ad81-399453d89115" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396726 1081 "the constant multiple property" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396726 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396726 1084 #uuid "d06cc1de-4117-5a41-b415-fe4170c4524d" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396727 1081 "the sum property" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396727 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396727 1084 #uuid "412b8550-fc4a-59a3-8ac2-9783dfa74f8c" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396728 1081 "the transitive prop