17592186397006 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397006 1077 "field-3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397006 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397007 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397006 1080 #uuid "7d0b526f-0a36-505c-bd42-a28d844cfb3c" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397007 1081 "x{e}^{-7x}" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397007 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397007 1084 #uuid "7665d218-e973-5ccf-a112-1b3cee61a4b6" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397008 1081 "{e}^{7x}" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397008 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397008 1084 #uuid "2a5fbc5d-982a-5e37-a3dc-84a876e64fc9" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397009 1081 "{e}^{-7x}" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397009 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397009 1084 #uuid "b7470fb6-388e-532f-839c-4263ebaddc37" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397010 1081 "x{e}^{7x}" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397010 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397010 1084 #uuid "9448a899-f5a3-5f84-b46b-10313439f92c" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397011 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397012 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397011 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397017 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397011 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397022 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397011 1069 "q-337488" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397011 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397011 1071 "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y=10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397011 1072 #uuid "5bf23900-2f3d-53c0-9448-69b2b01a2a2b" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397011 1074 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{5x})}^{′}-5(u{e}^{5x}) & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+5u{e}^{5x}-5u{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x=\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}\n$$\n\nour equation for $u$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\  & =10{e}^{-5x}(\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-5x}({e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}) \\\\  & =5+5{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =5+5{e}^{-10x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5+5{e}^{-10x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{5x} \\\\  & =5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397013 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397014 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397015 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397016 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1077 "field-3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397016 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397012 1080 #uuid "02bdb63b-0f09-5614-88a9-63938cc89b6d" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1081 "5x{e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397013 1084 #uuid "06d45bf0-b0d2-526d-9ee8-966bee2bf82f" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397014 1081 "{e}^{5x}-x{e}^{-5x}" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397014 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397014 1084 #uuid "f899948d-7d57-564f-9c17-dc1a4e8c1e4b" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397015 1081 "{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-5x}" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397015 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397015 1084 #uuid "cd83b01b-26af-5c69-90f0-dea06d731251" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397016 1081 "5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [1759218