he differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{3},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{3})^{′}=3{x}^{2}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(3{x}^{2})^{′}=6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(6x)-6x(3{x}^{2})+10({x}^{3})=4x.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{3}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{x}^{5}+B{x}^{2}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{x}^{5}+B{x}^{2}+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397311 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397312 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397311 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397313 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397311 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397311 1077 "field-1" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397311 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397313 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397311 1080 #uuid "609fd564-70da-56dd-9299-95878b1b6445" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397312 1081 "isn't" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397312 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397312 1084 #uuid "2f61fa9d-029d-5d0b-836f-7fd9c52c55bf" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397313 1081 "is" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397313 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397313 1084 #uuid "89a0b1c8-9210-56e2-99b9-b8e5988b2240" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397315 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397316 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397317 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397318 13194139533