e] [17592186397389 1069 "q-340655" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397389 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397389 1071 "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397389 1072 #uuid "42bf59e6-fc11-5187-a3f2-889c117ed67e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397389 1074 "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)=\\frac{{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{3t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-3t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{3t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-3t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+3)+(s-3)}{(s-3)(s+3)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (3,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-3,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(3,\\infty )\\cap (-3,\\infty )=(3,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>3.$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397391 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397392 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397393 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397394 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397395 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397396 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1077 "field-2" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397391 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397390 1080 #uuid "8fe74c7f-d29a-5023-a627-6b99c33c73b4" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397391 1081 "s>3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397391 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397391 1084 #uuid "6154e534-d5aa-500e-a111-0642cb1f5138" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397392 1081 "s\\ge 3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397392 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397392 1084 #uuid "90e7fe06-494b-5336-8647-cec5893e79b9" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397393 1081 "s\\ge 0" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397393 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397393 1084 #uuid "62aa5026-98f2-56d7-9078-cf1f425f67e3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397394 1081 "s>-3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397394 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397394 1084 #uuid "309debb7-997b-556d-8512-eacab65daa9e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [1759