-5508-b44e-84b13e3b138c" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397410 1081 "0" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397410 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397410 1084 #uuid "2134b48b-4f80-54ce-97ca-e2ded504ec18" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397411 1081 "-1" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397411 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397411 1084 #uuid "dfbe5295-15de-5429-ac7d-1288d0b2be34" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397412 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397413 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397412 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397416 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397412 1069 "q-340806" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397412 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397412 1071 "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397412 1072 #uuid "8afd30f6-9418-5f9f-a8dd-bdb05d34a03e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397412 1074 "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397413 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397414 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397413 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397415 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397413 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397413 1077 "field-1" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397413 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397415 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397413 1080 #uuid "35a58589-56cd-5637-b523-03f859fac5b6" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397414 1081 "even" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397414 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397414 1084 #uuid "d6fb8e02-c2ed-54c2-a769-c0f5e618e887" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397415 1081 "odd" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397415 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397415 1084 #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397416 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397417 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397416 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397418 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397416 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397416 1077 "field-2" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397416 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397418 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397416 1080 #uuid "52a06cf5-506a-5aec-8bcd-ea5d4fda8897" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397417 1081 "sine terms" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397417 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397417 1084 #uuid "34d21a9d-340e-5cb4-a005-7da885a8f606" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397418 1081 "cosine terms" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397418 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397418 1084 #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397419 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397420 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397419 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397424 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397419 1069 "q-340883" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397419 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397419 1071 "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ for $f(t)=u(t-2)+u(t-5),$ where $u$ is the unit step function.$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397419 1072 #uuid "94c1a445-854c-59cd-8bb7-f1e99e5361c5" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397419 1074 "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise functions $u(t-2)$ and $u(t-5),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t-2) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<2 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 2\\end{aligned} \\\\ u(t-5) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<5 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nu(t-2)+u(t-5)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<2 \\\\ 1,\\, & 2\\le t<5 \\\\ 2,\\, & t\\ge 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{5}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the second integral diverges for $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{5}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{2}^{5}+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{5}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-5s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}(0-{e}^{-5s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-5s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s},\\,s>0.\n$$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397420 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397421 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397420 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397422 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397420 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397423 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397420 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397420 1077 "field-2" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397420 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397423 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397420 1080 #uuid "3811f53b-a1af-5f49-ab19-7ecfb660367f" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397421 1081 "s>2" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397421 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397421 1084 #uuid "6d80295e-b463-5e7c-bf1a-e7d0d9f86058" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397422 1081 "s>5" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397422 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397422 1084 #uuid "08ab9610-98a7-5832-