ue] [17592186397489 1074 "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}2,\\, & t\\le 3 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\, & t>3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{t-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 1.$\n\nFor $s>1,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{3}+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{{e}^{(1-s)t}}{1-s})|}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{1-s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{(1-s)a}-{e}^{3(1-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{1-s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{3(1-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>1.$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397490 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397491 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397490 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397492 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397490 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397490 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397490 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397495 1319413953346