\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)+6\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)-9{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{3}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+9{\\pi }^{2}y=\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-6\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)+6\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)-9{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{3}}]+9{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-6\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x)+6\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x)=\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-6\\pi A=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ 6\\pi B=0\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}A=-\\frac{1}{27\\pi } \\\\ B=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=-\\frac{x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi x).\n$$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397651 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397652 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397651 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397653 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397651 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397654 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397651 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397655 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397651 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397651 1077 "field-1" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397651 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397655 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397651 1080 #uuid "6c917125-cff6-58cf-bd8e-53fff9587ed6" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397652 1081 "n=4" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397652 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397652 1084 #uuid "718e9566-c7c9-5a9a-b62c-206f45871768" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [1759218639