85 true] [17592186397737 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397738 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397737 1069 "q-49234" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397737 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397737 1071 "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[2{e}^{(k\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)/n}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}].$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397737 1072 #uuid "6a62fd18-f127-592a-8fe3-1cc5a47bb7fb" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397737 1074 "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=0.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}=\\frac{b-0}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{k}=\\frac{k\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=2{e}^{{x}_{k}}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}2{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[2{e}^{(k\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)/n}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397739 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397740 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397741 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397742 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397743 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397739 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397738 1080 #uuid "eb2a4470-ddb9-5a4f-aab9-d2401a7ffff8" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397739 1081 "$f(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397739 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397739 1084 #uuid "e499c456-6a1c-5152-933c-28134d048ffb" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397740 1081 "$f(x)={e}^{2x}$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397740 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397740 1084 #uuid "f947c798-bc89-571a-a666-d5ac5fe1b843" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397741 1081 "$f(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and $b=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397741 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397741 1084 #uuid "085d6ab0-e2f9-55ab-a353-c2e9ceb0a9dc" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397742 1081 "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397742 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397742 1084 #uuid "6da93e3c-bfd8-566a-bf85-bf589185d302" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397743 1081 "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397743 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397743 1084 #uuid "b72fbfe6-34a0-5341-a7d6-2590a001b91e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397744 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397745 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397744 1069 "q-66724" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397744 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397744 1071 "Given that $f(x)=2x+4,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nI. $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\nII. $x\\in (10,\\infty )$\nIII. $x\\in [-5,5)$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397744 1072 #uuid "8061fba9-94fb-59ab-bb67-c981e34d25e7" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397744 1074 "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $2$ and $y$-intercept $4,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/d3/d33314230419ec762bc4ad8603b2e6c3436461cd6b4b6fe4783d12a23d01b660.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (10,\\infty )$ and $x\\in [-5,5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397746 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397747 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397748 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397749 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397750 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397749 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397745 1080 #uuid "fb55a4d3-ef9d-5ba1-bc8d-64b5b8502eb6" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397746 1081 "I only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397746 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397746 1084 #uuid "2d49c863-bcca-5003-b60b-2402ac1bbc16" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397747 1081 "III only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397747 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397747 1084 #uuid "372a1527-fcb7-5e97-9214-ceab892980ce" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397748 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397748 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397748 1084 #uuid "89d11ef2-0ebb-56ef-85f5-eff24a1c20ef" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397749 1081 "I, II and III" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397749 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397749 1084 #uuid "6e8bd46d-8040-58fd-9418-5e14e16fd9fd" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397750 1081 "II only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397750 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397750 1084 #uuid "3ecd9f23-0f52-529d-9d3d-4b581fbbb61a" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397751 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397752 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397751 1069 "q-75640" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397751 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397751 1071 "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397751 1072 #uuid "2a792333-1cd7-596e-9f36-ea2d3aa5343e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397751 1074 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]=4[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=4{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}-4{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 4{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 4{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397753 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397754 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397755 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397756 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397757 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397756 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397752 1080 #uuid "5c4ee9d3-9826-59fa-81e1-d30802c66a1e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397753 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397753 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397753 1084 #uuid "af7cf2f2-a407-5089-94fd-71e651ca7964" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397754 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397754 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397754 1084 #uuid "4693ebba-1176-550d-b873-45ee14bc37e2" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397755 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397755 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397755 1084 #uuid "5f1a7171-2230-5136-86ce-13f9058caed9" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397756 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397756 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397756 1084 #uuid "0a130a78-a08b-509f-a270-8fb414ea9872" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397757 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397757 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397757 1084 #uuid "d231b096-e189-5829-b3fd-2b35888e10c4" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397758 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397759 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397758 1069 "q-75645" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397758 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397758 1071 "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397758 1072 #uuid "1429f843-5ee1-5edb-b1a8-4da2570633ca" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397758 1074 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=-2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=-2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397760 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397761 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397762 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397763 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397764 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397763 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397759 1080 #uuid "80b712db-bceb-5724-a93f-11876084e171" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397760 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397760 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397760 1084 #uuid "fc07a05b-0118-5252-b35b-ce58aaf33f50" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397761 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397761 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397761 1084 #uuid "013971a3-aab2-52a1-a19d-7a5ac0084ba8" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397762 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397762 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397762 1084 #uuid "142ba162-ec92-5e12-9e2e-f1802915a4bf" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397763 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397763 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397763 1084 #uuid "2d0e2276-3b1c-55bc-8e0d-1b1456cbdc62" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397764 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397764 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397764 1084 #uuid "7d2d7aa3-f1f3-582e-b408-82340acf0b62" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397765 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397766 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397765 1069 "q-78297" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397765 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397765 1071 "Which of the following represents a reflection across the $x$-axis?" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397765 1072 #uuid "1040f4bd-3d1a-5f7b-8b2b-4c581d4ad345" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397765 1074 "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/b9/b93bb91dae85a3e3b40a8d0ade3d4f420064aaa6926431fa7f664c977bb8fd59.png)" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397767 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397768 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397769 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397770 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397771 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397768 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397766 1080 #uuid "d53d07f6-e520-5ab9-8077-eda6c3ac37ba" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397767 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397767 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397767 1084 #uuid "c162ec8c-668b-5bfc-ab23-8423cf76c91f" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397768 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397768 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397768 1084 #uuid "62baa2db-7c19-5634-b5e6-1d42635e4fb5" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397769 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397769 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397769 1084 #uuid "e8c0ccfc-1a58-56d8-bf17-b789f1ca213c" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397770 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397770 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397770 1084 #uuid "c8045e89-1656-55f6-a0dd-d7b1b98bab9a" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397771 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397771 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397771 1084 #uuid "d3f965ef-6b47-527f-a571-556003d4b579" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397772 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397773 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397772 1069 "q-78302" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397772 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397772 1071 "Which of the following represents a reflection in the line $y=-x?$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397772 1072 #uuid "a51c70cd-319b-5de1-a71f-816af37c3370" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397772 1074 "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/4a/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397774 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397775 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397776 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397777 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397778 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397777 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397773 1080 #uuid "47512c4c-4d28-5025-9b41-fddc19cb1574" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397774 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397774 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397774 1084 #uuid "272ad4ce-b146-5a57-8c5a-5d1e1b3e79ba" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397775 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397775 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397775 1084 #uuid "b7fe5771-8880-5a10-a850-ea4baad6b72e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397776 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397776 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397776 1084 #uuid "c2191dbe-147e-5390-a126-2d6a0061ee2a" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397777 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397777 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397777 1084 #uuid "c22c0f50-7b0a-5358-91f1-6489ddb8ffdd" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397778 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397778 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397778 1084 #uuid "ace98a54-10d8-5584-91a9-8dc23cfa3eb3" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397779 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397780 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397779 1069 "q-94798" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397779 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397779 1071 "Let $S$ be the set of all polynomials in the real  variable $x$ with coefficients in $Q.$ Complete the following sentence: \n\n*$S$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397779 1072 #uuid "f0cbcdef-8d32-524c-bf12-b31a8feacf80" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397779 1074 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$S$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **multiplication of functions in  $S$ by real scalars is not closed.** *\n\nIndeed, let's consider, for example, the polynomial  $f(x)=x.$ Then $f\\in S$, but $\\sqrt{2}f(x)=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{ }x\\notin S$ because $\\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$\nOn the other hand: \n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- The zero function belongs to $S.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in S.$ $\\,✓$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397781 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397782 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397783 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397784 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397785 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397784 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186397780 1080 #uuid "